.TH MU2EDAQ-TOOLS 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-tools \- dispatcher for the Mu2e DAQ command line utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-tools
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-cluster
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-discovery\-timeout
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-color | \-\-no\-color ]
.I command
.RI [ command\-options ]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-tools
.BR \-V | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-tools
dispatches to subcommands registered in
.B mu2edaq_commandline_tools.cli.COMMANDS
and hands each one the effective configuration.
.PP
The configuration is resolved once per invocation from four sources, highest
precedence first: command-line options,
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_*
environment variables, one YAML file, built-in defaults.
An environment variable set to the empty string is treated as unset.
There is no
.I .env
layer.
.PP
The five global settings
.RB ( cluster ,
.BR discovery_timeout ,
.BR log_level ,
.BR log_dir ,
.BR color )
are resolved and shown by
.B config
but no current subcommand uses them: the package configures no logging,
performs no discovery and prints no colour.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Registered subcommands with their one-line help.
.TP
.B config \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
The effective configuration and the file it came from.
With
.B \-\-json
the output is
.BR "{\(dqconfig_file\(dq: path|null, \(dqvalues\(dq: {...}}" .
The CookieCode itself is never part of the configuration and is not shown.
.TP
.B version
Package version.
.TP
.B otsdaq
Read state and diagnostics from a running otsdaq instance, plus the
unrestricted
.B raw
request; see
.BR mu2edaq\-otsdaq (1).
.SH OPTIONS
Global options must precede the subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Use
.I FILE
as the only candidate.
A
.I FILE
that does not exist is not an error: the built-in defaults are used and
.B config
reports no file.
.TP
.BI \-\-cluster " NAME"
Default
.BR mu2edaq .
Unused.
.TP
.BI \-\-discovery\-timeout " SECONDS"
Default
.BR 2.0 .
Unused.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
One of DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR, CRITICAL.
Default
.BR INFO .
Unused.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-dir " DIR"
Default
.BR logs .
Unused by the tools.
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1)
recursively deletes the directory named by
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_DIR ;
the
.B \-\-log\-dir
option and the file key do not reach it.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Default on.
Unused.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print
.B mu2edaq\-tools
.I version
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Help, also per subcommand.
.SH FILES
The first existing regular file in this list is read:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\-c FILE                                  (if given, the only candidate)
$MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
\&./mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
\&./config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
<package>/config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml   (Python only)
~/.config/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml
/etc/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I <package>
is two directories above the installed
.IR config.py .
For the editable install that
.B bootstrap.sh
creates, that is the checkout, whose tracked
.I config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
always exists; the user and system files are then never reached by the Python
tools, while
.BR mu2edaq\-tools\-info (1)
does reach them.
.B \-c
and
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
undergo
.B ~
expansion here and not in the C++ library.
.PP
.B cmake \-\-install
writes the reference file to
.IR ${prefix}/etc/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml ,
which is on neither search path unless the prefix is
.IR / .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
Config file when
.B \-c
is absent.
A nonexistent path is skipped and the search continues.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CLUSTER ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_LEVEL ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_DIR ", " MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_COLOR
Override the matching file key; options override these.
.TP
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_INSTANCE ", " _GATEWAY_URL ", " _SLOW_CONTROLS_URL ", " _TFM_URL ", " _TIMEOUT ", " _VERIFY_TLS ", " _CA_BUNDLE ", " _COOKIE_FILE
Override the selected otsdaq profile; see
.BR mu2edaq\-otsdaq (1).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_OTSDAQ_COOKIE
CookieCode value; wins over any cookie file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The config file could not be read or is not a mapping, or PyYAML is missing.
A YAML syntax error is not caught and ends in a Python traceback, also with
status 1.
.TP
.B 2
No subcommand, or an invalid command line.
.PP
Subcommands return their own status; see
.BR mu2edaq\-otsdaq (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools config                     # which file, which values
mu2edaq\-tools \-c ./site.yaml config \-\-json
MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG=~/.config/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml mu2edaq\-tools config
mu2edaq\-tools otsdaq state \-\-instance crv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-otsdaq (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-tools\-info (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq_commandline_tools (3),
.BR mu2edaq_cli_core (3)
